{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793023897,"nonce":"qUJl3a5b4H2fJHRYuGcS6hwOjMI=","title":"Persist saved CRDT checkpoints in workspace Durable Objects","message":"Next durability slice under 52138fcda83502ec87679713955f7cf7c7f7e8654a0ef55ba60357bd0f22a904. The gateway currently persists metadata only; compute replacement loses its document-state disk. Add a versioned/checksummed complete native Save checkpoint, a safe native restore operation for replacement compute, and bounded Durable Object storage that commits a Save checkpoint before the hosted Save acknowledgment reaches the browser.\n\nScope checkpoints by logical workspace and native recovery generation; merge same-generation Yrs snapshots so reordered/concurrent saves cannot roll back a later save or revive deleted text. Do not merge snapshots from fresh compute baselines. Chunk storage values, maintain atomic manifests/quota accounting, preserve the previous checkpoint on errors, and cap in-flight Save tracking. Keep provider restore operations internal to the trusted control plane, not browser-forwarded. Test durable retention across object restart and compute destruction, restoration into fresh compute, normal browser collaboration, corrupt snapshots, storage boundaries and save acknowledgment ordering.\n\nThis is a saved-document checkpoint foundation, not complete DO document authority: unsaved update journaling, materializing the complete filesystem/tombstones, automatic VM recovery, leases/fencing, hibernation and production MSB provisioning remain open. Retain the existing browser context-generation fence until full continuity is proven. Prototype checkpoint bounds are independent of future account/tier retention policy.","files":null}]}